[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   Step 110 -- direction versus axis: decomposition of the
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   aphelion asymmetry.
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   Steps 061 and 108 measure the aphelion dipole as a DIRECTIONAL
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   statistic -- mean cos(theta) about the cap-declaration axis -- and
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   find it positive in every comet sample.  The slip field, by
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   contrast, is bipolar: step 089 found the residual proper-time
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   offset elevated toward BOTH ends of the axis (cos(2theta) basis).
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   These are different geometries.  A one-sided asymmetry (a flux, a
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   drift, a directional clustering) contributes to cos(theta); a
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   two-ended concentration about the axis line contributes to
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   |cos(theta)| and to cos(2theta) = 2 cos^2(theta) - 1.  This step
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   decomposes every comet sample's aphelion distribution into the
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   three moments under the identical tide-aware null:
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   T1  mean cos(theta)   -- the directional dipole (reproduces the
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   step-061/108 statistics as a machinery check)
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   T2  mean |cos(theta)| -- unsigned concentration about the axis
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   line: the signature a two-ended (bipolar) population would
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   carry
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   T3  mean cos(2theta)  -- the quadrupole moment: excess toward the
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   axis line over the equator
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   If the aphelion asymmetry is directional (one pole) while the
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   slip field is axisymmetric (two poles), the two channels measure
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   different aspects of the same structure: the direction of
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   approach versus the clock-sector field encountered in transit.
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   Samples: Warsaw spike, CODE class-1 matched, CODE-only, lpc
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   one-apparition, and the CometEls broad census + spike proxy --
[2026-09-20 12:20:55 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 110]   all reconstructed with the identical perih_dir machinery.
